{{!
    @template mod_aibranchedscenario/feedbackmark

    The mark on "Why this mattered".

    A light bulb stood here, which is the idea-and-tip mark every product uses for an
    optional aside. This is not an aside: it is the point the decision was testing, and the
    one paragraph on the screen the learner is meant to leave with. A mark that says "note
    this" rather than "here's a tip".

    Drawn once and shared, so the consequence screen, the debrief journey and the teacher's
    draft review cannot end up with three different marks on the same label.

    Example context (json):
    {
    }
}}
<svg class="aibs-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7.7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
    <path d="M10 5.9v4.7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"
          stroke-linecap="round"/>
    <circle cx="10" cy="13.9" r="1.05" fill="currentColor"/>
</svg>
